              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "গরু (gôru) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from gorūpa, \"cow-shaped\" (CDIAL 4313). It is go, \"cow\", + rūpa, \"shape\"."
